'''Legislative elections''' were held in [[Australia]] on [[10 November]] [[2001]]. All 150 seats in the [[Australian House of Representatives|House of Representatives]] and 40 seats in the 76-member [[Australian Senate|Senate]] were up for election. The conservative coalition of the [[Liberal Party of Australia|Liberal Party]], led by Prime Minister [[John Howard]] and the [[National Party of Australia]] led by [[John Anderson (Australian politician)|John Anderson]] was elected to a third three-year term, defeating the [[Australian Labor Party]] led by [[Kim Beazley, junior|Kim Beazley]]. Beazley resigned after the elections, his second defeat as Labor leader.

